<!-- ll-reveal demo — mirrors the upstream docs page
     (#/components/reveal). Upstream replays by remounting with a new key;
     here the Replay button calls restart(). The upstream `stagger` can't
     port (slotted children live in the page's style scope), so 03 gives
     each line its own ll-reveal with an incremental delay — that is the
     documented substitute. -->
<view class="demo">
  <view class="demo-title">Reveal</view>
  <view class="sec-desc">A wrapper that plays one of the theme's arrival keyframes — wipe, soak, drop, pop, toss — when its content comes into view.</view>

  <view class="sec">
    <view class="sub-h3">Default</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">The heading is drawn on left to right as it comes into view, once, with a marker tip writing it (nib). Replay mounts it again; on a long page it waits until you scroll to it.</view>
    <view class="rv-col">
      <ll-reveal id="rv-main" nib custom-style="font-size:44px;line-height:1.1">Drawn by hand, on the way in.</ll-reveal>
      <view class="sec-desc">Nothing is hidden from screen readers while it waits.</view>
      <view><ll-button size="sm" variant="outline" bind:tap="replayMain">Replay</ll-button></view>
    </view>
  </view>

  <view class="sec">
    <view class="sub-h3">Five arrivals</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">wipe, soak, drop, pop and toss, each one of the theme's keyframes. They play when they are on screen; scroll away and back with once turned off.</view>
    <view class="rv-row">
      <ll-reveal wx:for="{{effects}}" wx:key="name" effect="{{item.name}}" once="{{false}}" delay="{{item.delay}}">
        <ll-paper stock="{{item.stock}}" tilt="{{item.tilt}}" custom-style="width:128px;padding:16px;text-align:center">
          <text class="rv-script">{{item.name}}</text>
        </ll-paper>
      </ll-reveal>
    </view>
  </view>

  <view class="sec">
    <view class="sub-h3">A list that arrives line by line</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">A real use: stagger makes direct children arrive one after another, each drying like wet ink. Slotted children can't be animated from inside the component here, so each line carries its own ll-reveal and delay.</view>
    <view class="rv-list">
      <ll-reveal wx:for="{{features}}" wx:key="text" effect="soak" delay="{{item.delay}}" threshold="{{0.15}}">
        <view class="rv-line">
          <ll-checkbox checked="{{true}}" aria-label="{{item.text}}" />
          <text class="rv-line-text">{{item.text}}</text>
        </view>
      </ll-reveal>
    </view>
  </view>

  <view class="sr-only" aria-live="polite">{{said}}</view>
</view>
